							<a href="https://github.com/vidstack/captions" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-terracotta-500 hover:text-terracotta-600 underline">media-captions</a>
							is the caption parsing library from the
							<a href="https://vidstack.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-terracotta-500 hover:text-terracotta-600 underline">Vidstack</a> project
							(3,400+ GitHub stars). MIT licensed, actively maintained, and built specifically to address
							the gaps in native browser caption support.
						</p>
						<div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
							<div class="bg-parchment-100 border border-ink-200 p-5">
								<h4 class="font-semibold text-ink-900 mb-2">W3C WebVTT spec-compliant</h4>
								<p class="text-ink-600 text-sm font-serif">
									Follows the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/webvtt1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-terracotta-500 hover:text-terracotta-600 underline">W3C WebVTT specification</a>
									for parsing and rendering — correct cue settings, region positioning, and collision detection.
									Not a regex approximation, but a proper spec implementation.
								</p>
							</div>
							<div class="bg-parchment-100 border border-ink-200 p-5">
								<h4 class="font-semibold text-ink-900 mb-2">Accessibility-driven</h4>
								<p class="text-ink-600 text-sm font-serif">
									Built to meet FCC Communications and Video Accessibility Act requirements.
									Correct caption positioning matters for WCAG compliance — native browser <code class="font-mono text-xs">::cue</code> styling is too limited for
									accessible overlay rendering.
								</p>
							</div>
							<div class="bg-parchment-100 border border-ink-200 p-5">
